From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,dart: describe a DART's state
 across a deep sleep

A sleep that powers the SoC down resets every DART, and some of their
state comes from the boot loader, not from Linux:

- apple,dapf-ranges and apple,dapf-r20: the address filter the loader
  programs, to be written back before the consumer's firmware starts.
- A GAPF slice in place of the DAPF registers: the part of the fabric
  filter that guards a coprocessor CPU's power state, cleared to power
  that CPU down.
- apple,sleep-prepare, apple,sleep-restore and apple,sleep-restore-late:
  register writes around a sleep for a DART whose consumer gates itself
  and saves and restores it in its own order.
- apple,resume-tunable: the loader's tunables for a DART whose loader
  has already applied them, to be written back where a power-off lost
  them.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>

[j604 backport: reg-names: only gapf added (this binding has no Aurora auxiliary window)]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5

---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml | 66 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
index 003e253853..b81761f5a4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
@@ -65,13 +65,15 @@ properties:
       - description: DART registers
       - description:
           Address filter (DAPF) registers, which restrict the physical
-          addresses the DART lets its masters reach
+          addresses the DART lets its masters reach, or the slice of the
+          fabric filter (GAPF) that protects the power state of the
+          coprocessor CPU behind this DART, cleared to power that CPU down
 
   reg-names:
     minItems: 1
     items:
       - const: dart
-      - const: dapf
+      - enum: [dapf, gapf]
 
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
@@ -101,6 +103,54 @@ properties:
       may select a firmware-visible alias of the translation aperture.
       A consumer may further specify its own aperture in its binding.
 
+  apple,dapf-ranges:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint64-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: First address of a range
+        - description: Last address of a range
+    description:
+      The address filter the loader programs into the dapf registers, one
+      entry per range. A sleep that reaches the hardware clears it, and the
+      DART writes it back before its consumer's firmware starts again.
+
+  apple,dapf-r20:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      The last word of each filter entry, one per range in apple,dapf-ranges.
+      1 where absent.
+
+  apple,sleep-prepare:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: Register offset
+        - description: Value
+    description:
+      Register writes before a consumer that gates itself is told about a
+      firmware-driven system suspend. Needs apple,sleep-restore.
+
+  apple,sleep-restore:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: Register offset
+        - description: Value
+    description:
+      Register writes after such a suspend, before the translations are put
+      back. With this, the consumer saves and restores the DART around the
+      suspend, as the order relative to its firmware's start matters.
+
+  apple,sleep-restore-late:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: Register offset
+        - description: Value
+    description:
+      Register writes after the translations are back and before the streams
+      are enabled.
+
   apple,dma-offset:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint64
     description: >
@@ -142,6 +192,18 @@ properties:
       Tree by the bootloader and required to initialize dynamically powered
       DART instances.
 
+  apple,resume-tunable:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: Register offset
+        - description: Mask to be applied to the register value
+        - description: Bits to be set after applying the mask
+    description: >
+      The same tuples for a DART whose bootloader has already applied them,
+      written back where a power-off lost them, before its consumer's
+      firmware starts again.
+
   apple,bypass-sids:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
     minItems: 1
